 :status :design-only-unreviewed :authority :none
 :basis ["reviews/govone-offline-compile-qualification-plan-v2.edn" "reviews/govone-offline-compile-plan-review-v3.edn" "decisions/compiler-managed-temporary-file-preservation-clarification.edn"]
 :scope "Resolve v3 F1-F4 as a proposed, reviewable algorithm, not an assertion that any host capability exists. Prior records remain unchanged. No source authoring, inventory execution, snapshot, probe, build, runtime, spend or admission is granted. The existing 805306368-byte (768 MiB) shared dependency-cache allocation remains unchanged and read-only."
 :inventory {:admission "A separate permit must bind the exact roots, fixed GOOS/GOARCH, reviewer, source identities and limits below before static inventory; no Go tool or project code is run. Source authoring is independently admissible before inventory, subject to its own authorization."
             :roots ["owner module root /home/err/devel/orgs/mojomast/govone/.worktrees/feat/oikos-s6a-fixture-20261103" "/tmp/opencode/oikos-test-tools/go-1.27.1-ad3b4bab-a5d9-4328-8f90-e7b13f65cade/go" "/tmp/opencode/oikos-govone-deps-66a5b10a-0ac0-46f3-bf88-26763dd3d829/modcache" "/tmp/opencode/oikos-govone-deps-66a5b10a-0ac0-46f3-bf88-26763dd3d829/main-batch-snapshot/go.sum" "exact reviewed launcher and policy files"]
             :limits {:wall-seconds 300 :entries 500000 :read-bytes 2147483648 :manifest-bytes 67108864 :symlink-hops 16 :import-depth 128}
             :algorithm "Within those roots, lstat without following links; record sorted root-relative path, kind, mode, size, SHA-256 of every regular file and literal link target. Traverse every directory and hash every regular file, including all toolchain executables, tool data, standard library source, module archives and extracted files. Use descriptor-relative no-follow opens and recheck identities/metadata; escaped, absolute, looping, dangling or changing links and unsupported file kinds are unresolved. Never access outside a root. Exhaustion, read error or manifest overflow blocks; never silently truncate."
             :closure "Separately build a conservative source graph from both target directories: parse all Go files including tests and helpers, imports, embed patterns and matches, generated-file markers and already-present generated inputs, build tags and filename constraints for the pinned platform with CGO=0. Include all potentially applicable files if a constraint is ambiguous; report ambiguity. Resolve local imports and selected modules from static go.mod, go.sum, workspace metadata, replacements and reviewed selected-graph evidence; include standard-library imports and transitive edges. Record every missing path, unresolved import, unsupported directive, unsafe embed, ambiguous selection or external replacement. Whole-tree pins protect a superset but do not prove closure; unresolved cases block compile, not profile authoring."
             :custody "A separately authorized reviewed writer copies the inventoried conservative superset, private mod/sum and necessary toolchain/cache inputs into a private persistent snapshot; its destination, byte/inode capacity and retention are accounted before writing. Use no-follow descriptor-relative creation, exclusive names, preserve paths/modes/links only when safe, hash each copied file and independently compare full sorted manifests to stable source pre/post inventories. A source change, quota failure, partial copy or mismatch blocks sealing; retain partial evidence without cleanup. The writer exits and loses all write authority before an independently verified immutable snapshot or equivalent exclusive-writer custody is established; read-only bind and pre/post hashes alone are insufficient against external concurrent writes. No reader releases until custody, identity and manifests are verified. If immutable custody cannot be demonstrated, block."
             :manifest "Pin host architecture, toolchain tree and executable identities, loader/libraries if applicable, all graph edges, unresolved items, file metadata, input hashes, writer identity and custody proof. Hashes reported by v2 are historical, not current pins. Fresh independent review must close v7 findings and review both v8 tests."}
 :profile-source-ceiling {:authorization "Future source-only authorization may cover only the following roles, their minimal fixtures and exact integration changes; paths and baseline hashes must be fixed before editing. No second policy or ledger engine. Reuse the referenced v6 neutral controller and existing kernel interfaces, not a new event system."
                          :roles [:one-profile-launcher-and-dry-plan :existing-controller-minimal-profile-integration :one-exec-and-syscall-guard :one-snapshot-writer-and-manifest-verifier :one-persistent-store-and-retention-adapter :inert-neutral-fixtures-and-tests]
                          :review "Pin and independently review every changed source, configuration, fixture, trusted interpreter, dependency and host input. No owner source execution. Dry planning is a later separately admitted read-only operation, not a probe, snapshot or compile."
                          :dry-argv ["<pinned-reviewed-launcher>" "--dry-plan" "--profile" "<reviewed-profile.edn>" "--input-manifest" "<reviewed-input-manifest.edn>" "--host-manifest" "<reviewed-static-host-manifest.edn>" "--permit-template" "<reviewed-permit-template.edn>"]
                          :dry-inputs "Exact absolute roots and immutable identities; fixed platform; inventory and closure manifests with unresolved list; executable file identities; namespace, seccomp and Landlock policy; persistent stores and caps; cgroup settings; retention destination and independent observer identities; fixed argv/environment, deadlines and single-use permit template. The dry plan validates and prints a bounded deterministic action/refusal list only: no creating files, namespaces, stores or cgroups and no executing inputs. Missing identity, authority, capacity, control or unresolved closure is a refusal, not a successful qualification."}
 :exec-policy {:mechanism "Candidate Linux Landlock ABI supporting filesystem execute rights: before releasing an unprivileged child, trusted launcher opens and identity-verifies immutable regular executable files and installs a deny-by-default LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_EXECUTE ruleset with file-specific rules only for the pinned Go driver and the statically inventoried compiler, assembler and linker actually required by the fixed platform. Set no_new_privs and inherit restrictions across all threads and descendants. No directory-wide execute grant; do not grant execute to any writable path. Verify file-rule support and exact inode/mount identity under immutable custody; no pathname-only or seccomp-only authorization. Unsupported ABI, missing exact rule, substitution or unrecognized child is a hard stop."
               :transitions "Review Go driver source and platform tool tree statically to enumerate exact driver -> compile/asm/link child transitions, possible driver self-reexec, and executable digests; do not assume this list is exhaustive. Any additional child or dynamic interpreter requirement remains unresolved until separately reviewed and allowlisted. Deny scripts and interpreter-driven execution; reject script shebangs. Reject dynamic ELF unless its exact interpreter and libraries are pinned and the loader/direct-loader invocation and executable-mapping bypass are independently shown unable to run untrusted code; otherwise require reviewed static trusted binaries. No shell, native compiler, application executable, plugin or build hook is admitted; Go directives or tool behavior needing one fail closed. Both execve and execveat, including descriptor-based execution, must be covered by identity-bound kernel enforcement; deny memfd and executable writable mappings or otherwise prove they cannot bypass it."
               :other-controls "Independently reviewed architecture-specific seccomp filter denies alternate ABIs, network including AF_UNIX and socketpair, io_uring, namespace/mount operations, ptrace, escape and dangerous metadata syscalls; explicitly review required metadata operations rather than asserting blanket denial is compatible with Go. Minimal reviewed proc/dev, no writable inherited descriptors, host sockets, credentials or host filesystem writes. Review remaining channels, loader and open descriptors. Kernel-enforced read-only input views and no external writers are both required. CGO_ENABLED=0, offline only; no fallback or shared-cache mutation."}
 :storage {:design "Candidate only: two disjoint pre-existing, persistently backed, kernel-enforced quota domains on a filesystem whose independent byte AND inode accounting, including metadata and links, is proven by the neutral qualification. Cache domain is at most 268435456 bytes; other domain is at most 268435456 bytes; their disjoint sum is at most 536870912 bytes. There is no nested quota and no reliance on a parent quota aggregating a child. If existing delegated quota authority or accounting is unavailable or metadata cannot be bounded and evidenced, refuse; no sudo, root, loop device, mount or quota change is implied. Alternative mechanisms require a revised reviewed profile."
           :placement "Only GOCACHE writes in cache domain. GOTMPDIR, TMPDIR, HOME, private mod/sum, final binaries, captured logs and output manifests live in the other domain. Reserve fixed reviewed byte/inode headroom there for bounded logs and preservation manifests before release, protected from compiler consumption by a separately enforceable quota or preallocated durable capacity; if protection cannot be proved, block. Snapshot copies and neutral artifacts use separately authorized persistent bounded capacity and are not hidden in the build-store accounting. No other writable descriptor or path is exposed."
           :enforcement "Bind exact quota identifiers, backing filesystem, kernel limits, inode limits and accounting semantics in the future permit. Controller observes quota state but cannot substitute polling, RLIMIT_FSIZE or du for enforcement. Account hardlinks, directories, metadata, sparse files and rename/cross-domain behavior; deny or prove bounded any operation that escapes accounting. ENOSPC, EDQUOT, inode exhaustion, missing reserve, unexplained writes or inability to persist evidence stops the batch, prevents the second command and is failure, not an automatic retry. Cgroup memory is a separate 1 GiB ceiling, never counted as disk enforcement."
           :unknown "If no nonprivileged enforceable persistent store is presently known, the next separately admitted neutral capability test is whether an already delegated pair of disjoint persistent quota domains provides these kernel byte/inode/metadata limits and protected evidence reserve without privileged setup. Unknown is not impossible or passed. Failure blocks this design; it does not authorize escalation."}
 :lifecycle {:limits {:wall-seconds 240 :memory-bytes 1073741824 :tasks-max 128 :cpu-percent 100 :combined-output-bytes 1048576 :cache-bytes 268435456 :aggregate-store-bytes 536870912}
             :control "Use the reviewed neutral controller as reference only. Before release, independent manager evidence records configured cgroup and quota identities; independent kernel readback verifies cgroup membership, memory/pids/cpu limits, quota settings and guard state; a third lifecycle observer anchors process identity using pidfds and records all descendants. Evidence must name independent sources, timestamps and identities, not merely controller assertions. One shared deadline and output cap cover both commands; output overflow is a failure and terminates the group after retaining the bounded prefix and explicit overflow evidence."
             :shutdown "On first failure, timeout, overflow, forbidden action, lost observer or quota failure, stop launches, identity-anchor termination of the original cgroup and descendants, reap, and independently verify kernel cgroup emptiness within a fixed permit-bound observation deadline. If control or proof is lost, mark failed/indeterminate and retain stores and evidence; no retry, cleaner or teardown that could destroy outputs. Neutral qualification must demonstrate positive and negative controls and process/cgroup lifecycle; it cannot establish actual Go behavior."
             :preservation "Persistent quota stores outlive sandbox, launcher and supervisor; do not use a volatile tmpfs as sole backing. Compiler may perform ordinary cleanup of its own internal temporaries under the user's clarification; no external cleaner, scratch deletion or cache deletion is allowed. Final binaries are written directly to named persistent paths, never run, then closed, hashed and independently inventoried with bounded stdout/stderr, exit status, input manifests, control/kernel/lifecycle evidence and a completeness/failure manifest. Fsync files and parent directories and independently reopen and verify identities and hashes before sandbox teardown. The permit must identify the persistent retention location, owner and capacity; retained artifacts remain subject to verified-backup-before-cleanup."
             :interruption "At timeout, failed compile or kill, preserve any partial binary as partial, logs and all available evidence; never label it successful. If supervisor crashes, an independently supervised recovery path keeps persistent stores intact and marks the run indeterminate until cgroup emptiness and inventory can be established. If host shutdown interrupts writes, after restart retain the same stores and recover only fsynced verifiable bytes, mark incomplete or missing evidence indeterminate, and never claim full preservation or success. If durable retention cannot be established before release, refuse compile. No deletion is authorized even after successful verification."}
 :neutral {:status :not-admitted :count "At most one separately permitted finite batch for the exact reviewed profile and host; no retries or expansion."
           :argv ["<pinned-reviewed-launcher>" "--neutral-qualify" "--profile" "<reviewed-profile.edn>" "--permit" "<one-shot-neutral-permit.edn>" "--fixture-manifest" "<reviewed-inert-fixtures.edn>"]
           :coverage "Inert fixtures only, no Go or project code: independently check persistent delegated quota byte/inode/metadata/link enforcement, protected evidence reserve, immutable writer exclusion, exec identity and denied substitutions including execveat, seccomp and descriptor hygiene, cgroup pre-release kernel readback, descendant termination and persistent retention across permitted teardown. Negative networking checks deny before communication. Preserve neutral evidence and partial artifacts under the same limits and rules. A result qualifies only the exact neutral controls, not compile viability. All capability tests require a distinct permit; no probe is authorized here."}
